<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds recovered on Friday from Thursday's decline, helped by an improvement in U.S. stocks and bonds, dealers said.</p>
<p>Confidence returned to the market after Wall Street and the Treasury bond steadied. There were no new domestic factors, as the market had expected the Bank of Spain to hold its key rate steady at 6.25 percent as it did.</p>
<p>Spanish fundamentals and market tone continued positive, with the yield spread to Germany hovering beneath 100 basis points amid views Spain would meet economic convergence criteria for the common European currency.  </p>
<p>The Spanish market will be closed on Monday for a holiday.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
